~ initialize_local_variables
do Variables.add_local("childhood", false)
do Variables.add_local("family", false)
do Variables.add_local("day", false)
do Variables.add_local("yday", false)
do Variables.add_local("lover", false)
do Variables.add_local("dreams", 0)
do Variables.add_local("fingers", false)
do Variables.add_local("toes", false)
do Variables.add_local("breathe", false)
do Variables.add_local("eyes", false)
do Variables.add_local("questions", 0)
=> start

~ start
A frail fragment: [speed=0.2][shake rate=10.0 level=2]Hold on to me. 
A frail fragment: [speed=0.2][shake rate=10.0 level=2]Do not let go.
A frail fragment: [speed=0.2][shake rate=10.0 level=2]...
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]You went to bed early tonight, feeling especially tired for no particular reason. Long day at work, perhaps?
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]Staring at the ceiling, you didn't move an inch as hours passed you by. It's way past midnight, now. You're almost asleep, half-thinking, half-dreaming. 
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]What about? => about

~ about
A frail fragment: ...
- My childhood. [if Variables.get_var("childhood") == false]
	A frail fragment: Memories forgotten, unwillingly unearthed.[do Variables.set_var("childhood", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	A frail fragment: Buildings, larger than life. Planes, cars, buses, loud. Food you wouldn't eat. Leftovers?
	A frail fragment: A friend? Just not a very good one. Wouldn't ever let you play with their toys.
	A frail fragment: Were you poor? No. Not really. But it sure felt that way. 
	A frail fragment: Another friend. A dog. Gone too soon. 
	A frail fragment: Your parents loved you. They did all they could, but you resented them for it.
	A frail fragment: Eh, you can't blame yourself. You were young. Kids are pricks. 
	A frail fragment: For the first time in forever, you're able to push the guilt aside.
	A frail fragment: What else? => about
- My family. [if Variables.get_var("family") == false]
	A frail fragment: Mom. Dad. Two older brothers. A sister. Younger?[do Variables.set_var("family", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	A frail fragment: Voices. Whispers. Screams. A handful of blurred faces and hushed voices. 
	A frail fragment: They call to you. It gets louder and quieter in equal measure. 
	A frail fragment: Shame on you, they say. Then they leave. 
	A frail fragment: Can you really not remember them? 
	A frail fragment: You've had this dream before, a few times. But these people mean nothing to you, now.
	A frail fragment: What else? => about
- The day it all began. [if Variables.get_var("day") == false]
	A frail fragment: The day all what began?[do Variables.set_var("day", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	A frail fragment: Oh. Right. 
	A frail fragment: You vaguely remember crows filling up the sky. Could barely see anything anymore. Your parents thought it was an eclipse. 
	A frail fragment: Then they were gone. The sky turned red, a lot of people died, you survived. End of story. 
	A frail fragment: You were too young to understand what was happening. Or to remember much else. 
	A frail fragment: The Cullings, as people have fittingly named them, have been a thing ever since. 
	A frail fragment: You were placed in foster care, then left the day you turned eighteen. That's about it. Right?
	A frail fragment: What else? => about
- Yesterday. [if Variables.get_var("yday") == false]
	A frail fragment: The usual. Helped around any way you could. Got paid for it. Came home.[do Variables.set_var("yday", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	A frail fragment: Watched some TV. A new tape your coworker gave you. Some old show from way back when, about a serial killer heartthrob. Complete non-sense. 
	A frail fragment: It was nice of her, though. She's always nice to you. Always greets you with a smile.  
	A frail fragment: Got through a couple of episodes, then went to bed. 
	A frail fragment: ...Or was that the day before?
	A frail fragment: Maybe it was a dream you had.
	A frail fragment: You try your hardest to remember. You can't. 
	A frail fragment: What else? => about
- A... lover? [if Variables.get_var("lover") == false]
	A frail fragment: NO. [do Variables.set_var("lover", true)]
	#[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_boom")]
	A frail fragment: What else? => about
- Just... stop. Give in. [if Variables.get_var("dreams") >= 2]


~ dream
A frail fragment: It all feels rather... generic. Impersonal. These thoughts, or dreams, leave you cold and empty. No twitching muscles, no elevated heart-rate, no sweat.
A frail fragment: Are these bland memories really yours? 
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]They're all brought to a stop by... something. A gust of wind you can barely feel. 
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]You try to cling to them but they're... gone, somehow. 
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]It's cold, all of a sudden. Colder than you've ever felt.
A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]Are you awake now?
- Yes.
	A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]How can you be sure? => react
- No. 
	A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]That's right. You aren't. Wake up. => react 
- I... don't know?
	A frail fragment: [speed=0.6]Time to find out. => react

